  "query_preview": "/Monday through Friday/...\nWith models slightly out of phase later in the long term, and\nthe only chance of precipitation associated with a weak low over\nSouthern California, the bulk of the long term forecast is\nfocused on temperature trends as the synoptic pattern shifts.\nMonday afternoon through Tuesday evening, the weak Californian\nlow moves across the Southwestern US. During this time, we \noccupy a slightly moistened northeastern quadrant between the \nlow and zonal flow to our north. Dynamics will favor development\nof showers in Central and Eastern Idaho Monday and Tuesday \nafternoons. The chance of precipitation each afternoon is only\n10%. Otherwise, that zonal flow to the north moderates\ntemperatures, holding them steady at 5 degrees above normal for\nmost of the long term. Slight warming on Thursday is expected as\nhigh pressure builds ahead of a strong Alaskan low pressure\nsystem. This low pressure system moves through British Columbia\nlate next week, with model variation on the exact track keeping\nour forecast low confidence that far out.",
